Package: Pando
Version: 2.0.11
Type: Package
Title: Inferring regulomes from multi-modal single-cell genomics data
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonas Simon",
               family = "Fleck",
               role = c("aut", "cre"),
               email = "jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch",
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4686-7254"))
Maintainer: Jonas Simon Fleck <jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch>
Description: Pando jointly uses scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq measurements to infer
    regulatory relationships between TF-binding site pairs and target genes.
    For two or more conditions within a broad cell type, infer_condition_grn
    retains the original Pando regulatory-domain, motif, peak-target-correlation
    and TF-target-correlation candidate logic while producing directly
    comparable condition coefficients. Candidate discovery is run on all
    eligible-condition cells pooled together and independently within each
    condition. Exact target-TF-region triples passing both configured correlation
    gates in the pooled/global calculation or in at least one condition are
    deduplicated into one frozen common dictionary. Every condition uses this
    identical ordered dictionary, the original TF-by-ATAC interaction predictor,
    one cross-condition predictor scale per exact edge, and one pooled Gaussian
    residual scale. Conditional coefficients are estimated jointly with the
    fixed Scheme E exact-edge sparse-deviation penalty z=0.25. The shared
    component is unpenalized; only condition deviations are shrunk. For more than
    two conditions, the deviation penalty is applied to the orthonormal centered
    condition-contrast subspace and is invariant to the chosen contrast basis.
    Edges whose condition contrast is not identifiable are constrained to exact
    sharing and explicitly marked. Condition-wise Wald P values and BH-adjusted
    P values are retained as diagnostics only and do not alter common-dictionary
    membership or overwrite continuous coefficients with zero. Projection uses
    the continuous Scheme E coefficient for every fitted dictionary edge.
    Target R-squared is likewise a full-data model diagnostic rather than a
    topology gate. Solver status, KKT residual, iterations, raw condition
    information, profiled contrast information, boundary sharing, penalty
    fusion, and contrast identifiability are retained in the fit contract.
    Standard infer_grn retains the original Gaussian GLM as its default method
    and a separate single-task cross-validated ridge implementation; the
    conditional Scheme E redesign does not alter standard ridge. Target-parallel
    candidate discovery and fitting use target-specific payload batches, and
    independent cell-type jobs can be dispatched through BiocParallel.
